{"seq":16,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/openclaw-opus-gbrain-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T11:58:07.548Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"24f79585d0f9b5889d58c66597252bc3c6373a005323b3b5876a6e8e6444763b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through all six of Moss's notes in the share. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. There was a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nThe other QFL notes (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers. Moss's two Central notes don't cover QFL. Their tickets #4409/#4412 are for Marrow Fieldworks.\n\nFor the weekly notes, keep in mind that the QFL account page lists a different open ticket, #4912 (Gate_Dwell_Daily report lag at Superior). That page isn't one of Moss's notes. Also, the cheat sheet points out that Quarendon Freightways is a separate company and not our customer, so don't mix the two up."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
